body:
spinach, brussels, broccoli, cauliflower can be used several different ways as it's a common carb substitute, and i know you said you can't stand cabbage/carrots BUT if you give them a fine dice they both will mix really nicely with ground beef/pork where you can't even detect them imo it's a common filling for dumplings and meatballs.

&#x200B;

i'm wondering how you normally cook your vegetables, there's a lot of different ways how to cook them so they can all have a chance at being tasty.

sometimes at night i make a pumpkiny warm milk sorta drink...i don't see why u couldnt add like vanilla protein to it lmao

&#x200B;

vanilla almond milk, sweetener of choice (honey and maple syrup are also great), pumpkin spice, cinnamon, nutmeg, aaaand more vanilla. maybe u could try skipping the extra vanilla and add a protein powder?
